==Strategy==
An easy stage, all things considered. Despite the enemy composition seeming rather unpleasant, spamming piercing damage like [[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Talented Housewife Cat]] and [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] will net you a frictionless victory, given good enough meatshielding with [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]] and [[Jetpack Cat (Rare Cat)|Jetpack Cat]]. Be careful if you bring [[Master Uril (Special Cat)|Esoteric Uril]] to this stage, as Techn-old Hyena has counter-surge; you may be better off sticking to using just [[Master of Logic Newtone (Special Cat)|Newtone]].

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Celestial Child Luna (Uber Rare Cat)|Salvation's Daughter Lunacia]]: Luna makes dealing with Ostromeda a lot easier. While her Freeze isn't nearly as effective against Techn-Old Hyena, her DPS still makes quick work of them.
*Super-Backliners like [[Lucifer the Fallen (Uber Rare Cat)|Almighty Lucifer]] or [[The Grateful Crane (Uber Rare Cat)|Supernova Cosmo]] can hit all enemies from a safe distance.
*[[Mizli (Uber Rare Cat)|Mizunade]]: While Mizunade does a great job at crowd-controlling Commander Ostromeda and Techn-Old Hyena, you do need to be wary of the latter's [[Surge Attack#Counter-Surge|Counter-Surges]], so if you're using her, try to run Warp/Surge immune meatshields and attackers.
*[[Bora (Uber Rare Cat)|Bazibastra]]: Bazibastra's role here is extremely straightforward. Send them out, keep them well protected and watch as they nuke all of this stage's Alien enemies.

